WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.680
On most blockchains,

00:00:01.680 --> 00:00:03.840
anyone who knows an address can read its

00:00:03.840 --> 00:00:06.560
balance and every amount it paid.

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:09.840
Nulo shows two balances for each token.

00:00:09.840 --> 00:00:11.480
Your private balance:

00:00:11.480 --> 00:00:13.240
only you can see it.

00:00:13.240 --> 00:00:14.880
Your public balance:

00:00:14.880 --> 00:00:16.080
anyone can see it,

00:00:16.080 --> 00:00:18.200
like a balance on Ethereum.

00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:19.640
Your private balance is a

00:00:19.640 --> 00:00:21.200
set of encrypted notes,

00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:23.600
like cash in sealed envelopes.

00:00:23.600 --> 00:00:25.400
The network keeps a fingerprint

00:00:25.400 --> 00:00:26.453
of each note,

00:00:26.453 --> 00:00:29.920
and a sealed copy only its owner can open.

00:00:29.920 --> 00:00:33.920
Say you pay 3.50 from a note worth 5.

00:00:33.920 --> 00:00:36.720
Nulo spends that note and makes new ones:

00:00:36.720 --> 00:00:39.440
3.50 for the person you pay,

00:00:39.440 --> 00:00:42.240
and 1.50 change for you.

00:00:42.240 --> 00:00:43.520
In a private payment,

00:00:43.520 --> 00:00:46.080
the record shows that something was spent.

00:00:46.080 --> 00:00:47.920
It does not show which note,

00:00:47.920 --> 00:00:49.360
or how much.

00:00:49.360 --> 00:00:50.880
Moving money to your public

00:00:50.880 --> 00:00:52.373
balance is your choice,

00:00:52.373 --> 00:00:54.880
and the public side records the amount.

00:00:54.880 --> 00:00:56.720
Nulo labels each balance,

00:00:56.720 --> 00:00:58.880
so you always know which is which.
